#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:2
msgid "Hotplug support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:4
msgid ""
"Hotplug support gives snaps the ability to integrate with Linux's [USB "
"hotplugging](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/v4.13/driver-api/usb/"
"hotplug.html) and Udev device management subsystem. This enables snaps to "
"recognise specific classes of device and create corresponding system slots "
"when a device is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:6
msgid ""
"Developers wishing to add hotplug functionality to their own interfaces "
"should see {ref}`Developing hotplug interfaces <interfaces-developing-"
"hotplug-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:8
msgid ""
"Initially, only USB serial port adapters using the {ref}`serial-port "
"interface <interfaces-serial-port-interface>` are supported. Other types of "
"device, such as USB cameras, will be added in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:10
msgid ""
"In addition to creating a slot, snapd's hotplug support also remembers "
"connections. If the device is unplugged, its slot disappears from the "
"system. When the device is reconnected, its slot and connections are "
"restored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:12
msgid ""
"*snapd* tracks devices by matching specific udev attributes. This means that "
"even when a device is reconnected with a different udev path, such when it "
"uses a different USB port or gets a non-deterministic enumeration by the "
"kernel, it is still recognised as the old device by snapd and its old "
"connections are restored with updated attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:14
msgid "Enabling hotplug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:16
msgid ""
"Hotplug is currently an experimental feature that needs to be enabled. First "
"ensure you have a recent snapd installed, either via the core snap or the "
"snapd snap, at least 2.39."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:18
msgid "Then enable hotplug support with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:20
msgid "sudo snap set system experimental.hotplug=true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:24
msgid ""
"You will need to either restart snapd (with `sudo systemctl restart snapd`, "
"for example), or reconnect USB devices to initiate hotplug processing for "
"connected devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:26
msgid "Hotplug slots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:28
msgid ""
"The name of a hotplug slot is typically derived from a device’s udev "
"attributes, such as `NAME`, `ID_MODEL_FROM_DATABASE` and `ID_MODEL`. If "
"multiple devices of the same type are connected, a numeric suffix could be "
"added to make their names unique."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:30
msgid ""
"For example, a USB serial adapter from Future Technology Devices "
"International (FTDI) with a model name of *FT232R_USB_UART*, will create the "
"following slot for the system snap when connected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:32
msgid ""
"$ snap interface serial-port\n"
"name:    serial-port\n"
"summary: allows accessing a specific serial port\n"
"slots:\n"
"  - core:ft232rusbuart\n"
"\n"
"$ snap connections system\n"
"Interface           Plug            Slot                Notes\n"
"[...]\n"
"serial-port         -               :ft232rusbuart      -\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:45
msgid "Current limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:47
msgid ""
"Along with only supporting USB serial port adapters, hotplug is restricted "
"to devices that provide a specific set of udev attributes; name, vendor "
"identifier and/or serial number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:49
msgid ""
"These attributes are needed to identify and track devices. This isn’t "
"normally a problem for branded devices, but it may cause issues with "
"unbranded devices. Without the required attributes, a device cannot be "
"supported and will be ignored when connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/hotplug-support.md:51
msgid ""
"There is also no easy way to list connected devices and their corresponding "
"slots. This limitation will be addressed in an upcoming snapd release."
msgstr ""
